A compiler

The `Compiler` holds the `Lexer`, the `Parser`, the `Checker` and the
`Code generator`. `Source` goes to the `Lexer`, the `Lexer` gives tokens to the
`Parser`, the `Parser` gives a tree to the `Checker`, and the `Checker` gives
the tree to the `Code generator`, which writes the `Binary`.
---
Compiler { Lexer, Parser, Checker, Code generator }
Source -> Lexer
Lexer -> Parser: tokens
Parser -> Checker: tree
Checker -> Code generator: tree
Code generator -> Binary: write
